// name :
"P3853285940" "The Fate of All Men"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BaB 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3045375045" "Back Alley Brawler's Investigation"
// DetailString :
"P2968453389" "You defeated Back Alley Brawler and retrieved a data pad that was on his person. It detailed the investigation that he was performing regarding the whereabouts of Darrin Wade. It seems that something is going on regarding Darrin Wade and Rularuu, a fact you're now <i>very</i> well aware of after walking through the basement of the bar in Port Oakes.<br><br>Something isn't right here, but it doesn't come as too much of a surprise to learn that Darrin Wade was hiding something from you.<br><br>You can hear some sort of commotion upstairs in the bar. You'll have to see what's going on there, then find the location of Darrin Wade's lair. He's going to regret hiding something from you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Tunnels 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P832897454" "Port Oakes Tunnel System"
// DetailString :
"P1971726574" "You received a detailed map of the tunnel system located beneath Port Oakes. You look over the map to see where Blackbeard's tavern is located.<br><br>After a few minutes, you're able to figure out how to get into the tunnels that Darrin Wade seemed to be protecting; it will require you going into one of the older sewer networks in Port Oakes, unfortunately."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P831588365" "The Secrets of Cimerora"
// DetailString :
"P3665761369" "You found in the chest piles of writing regarding Cimerora, possibly collected over several years. You read it over, all of the information coming together to form an interesting conclusion.<br><br>It begins a woman named Sister Airlia, who was able to enchant Imperious, the former ruler of Cimerora. He would listen to everything she would say.<br><br>Romulus Augustus, an enemy to Cimerora, had his armies driven back by what Wade noted as 'time-travelling meddlers'. He made one last attempt to attack Cimerora, this time aided by monsters called the Talons of Vengeance. Wade makes a note, saying he's not sure why the Talons attacked Cimerora.<br><br>Romulus Augustus was defeated one final time by a time traveler. However, due to his powers, he was nearly unkillable, much like Imperious. Sister Airlia, however, had a plan, one that she had been working on for many years and which caused her skin and body to become deformed.<br><br>Sister Airlia created a powerful magical ritual that could nullify the essences of Imperious and Romulus. The ritual would then use the built up power to <i>kill</i> the two.<br><br>Sister Airlia convinced Imperious that if Cimerora was going to be safe from Romulus, Imperious would have to give up his life. Imperious accepted, and the ritual was performed at the top of the Sybil Temple. Imperious and Romulus were killed in the ensuing ritual, ending the reign of Imperious and the terror of Romulus.<br><br>On the bottom of the last page is a comment by Wade, stating that he had finally gathered all the components needed to match Airlia's ritual. You realize, now, that if this is true, Darrin Wade has the power to <i>kill</i> Statesman!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2792201586" "Summoning Rularuu"
// DetailString :
"P1176966148" "You looked through the remains of Darrin Wade's library to find any sort of important information. You find multiple journals and read them over, looking for anything important. It's odd, that Darrin Wade would leave such important items here. Wade must believe it's too late for his plan to be stopped, or he <i>wants</i> someone to know what he's doing.<br><br>You see that over the past ten years, Darrin Wade has been working on a magic spell that would break the dimensional barrier between this world and the Shadow Shard, the dimension where Rularuu is imprisoned. Wade makes notes that this mission is pure suicide without proper preparation, as Rularuu will destroy all of existence if he is to be released.<br><br>Wade, however, decided to come up with a plan. To merge with Rularuu and take <i>control</i> of the creature by summoning small portions of him into this world. If he could take over Rularuu piece by piece, he could ascend and become something more than a super-powered individual. Darrin Wade's goal was... or rather, <i>is</i>, to become a new Rularuu. He makes note that once this happens, he can have full control over the world. No longer would have to live in a world where all of the knowledge he has amounts to nothing against a dumb oaf who happened to be blessed with super strength.<br><br>The final page in his last journal details that he's gathered all the items needed to bring Rularuu into this world, a trio of artifacts called the 'items of power'. There is fresh writing at the bottom, as if Wade wrote the last part mere hours ago. He writes to Positron, saying that it's far too late to stop his plan, but that he's welcome to try. Wade says that today everything will come together, and it will be the beginning of end of this old existence as the world knows it. It looks like Wade didn't wager on you finding this instead of Positron."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3291717823" "Luring our Statesman"
// DetailString :
"P2664733509" "You dig through another one of Wade's chests for any information. You find a letter, addressed to Positron.<br><br>'Dear Positron,<br><br>Did my trick in the tunnels fool you? Or did you try to butter up the Arbiters to get information about me? Oh, what about my journals? I hope you were able to piece together the research I did on Cimerora. It's very sloppy, but then again, I have been working on this for nearly a decade.<br><br>Anyway, today is when all of the pieces snap together. To be honest, I'm excited to see it happen. My hands are trembling slightly at the very thought.<br><br>Today, I will kill Statesman, and then, I will kill you. There is still more to my plan after this, and I can't risk having you alive. I was going to ask {HeroName} to take care of you, but I didn't want to put {Hero.gender=male him|her} at further risk, not after the whole incident in Warburg.  I have the final obelisk belonging to that idiotic ghost, Alastor. It's tucked away, safe and sound; I won't be revealing <i>that</i> part of my plan.<br><br>I'm assuming you were held up by the numerous road blocks I put in your way to finding my base. As we speak, Statesman is flying towards the modern day ruins of Cimerora. I've sprinkled information for him to find about my whereabouts. He doesn't know a thing about the ritual though, which is why it'll be that much more exciting when I <i>kill</i> him.<br><br>Of course, the ritual won't work on <i>you</i>. Or anyone else, for that matter. The components are all destroyed once it's used, thanks to how poorly Sister Airlia formed the ritual. I'll just kill you with Statesman's powers, and if that doesn't suffice... well, there are plans.<br><br> I'll need to get going, my Rularuu guests have arrived. I'll look forward to killing you, {HeroName}.<br><br>Regards,<br><br>Darrin Wade."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ClueTLDR 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1259484816" "Darrin Wade's Plan"
// DetailString :
"P2325281266" "You found out in Darrin Wade's lair that he plans on summoning Rularuu into this world and taking over the monster. Wade also plans on using an ancient Cimeroran ritual to <i>kill</i> Statesman. All of this seems to stem from his desire to become more powerful than anyone in this existence. You have to wonder what caused Wade to be like this. Was the idea of being normal in a world of super-powered beings too much for him to handle? Even with all his magical artifacts, Darrin Wade still felt that he was just a regular man.<br><br>Whether or not Statesman dies is irrelevant, though of course, getting the killing blow on him would immortalize you. If Darrin Wade is planning on becoming Rularuu, there isn't much room for <i>you</i> in that equation, even if his plan is that you both rule side by side. If Wade is in the ruins of Cimerora, then that's where you'll be going next."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL8_9_Issue1_Arc_5_Villain_Arc_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P4146286575" "Piece of Statesman's Cape"
// tDetailString :
"P3608891921" "You took a piece of Statesman's cape, a souvenir of the when the legend died. News stations all over the world were broadcasting the news of Statesman's death the night after it happened. The Freedom Phalanx wanted to keep it a secret, but it seems someone leaked the information to the press. One of the gloomier newscasts called Statesman's death...<br><br><b>The Fate of All Men</b><br><br>The news reported that the man responsible for Stateman's death was Darrin Wade. Somehow, there are also reports about your involvement in the whole matter, that you stopped an investigation being performed by Back Alley Brawler. News reports also begin rumors that you and Darrin Wade actually fought each other over Statesman's dead body.  Your reputation is being debated amongst the pundits, some of them wondering if now at this point, the world must rely on a villain to save it.<br><br>It wouldn't be the first time you've had to do something for the greater good, but who says that you necessarily have to? Statesman's dead, and Paragon has a huge hole in its defenses. This is a time brimming with opportunity; it's just a matter of what opportunity you'll be taking."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - WadeFinal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3800029564" "Well, {HeroName}, I'm a little surprised to see <i>you</i> here."
// Answer Text :
"P4052239071" "I found your lair, Wade. Guess what I discovered."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3915993181" "I can only assume from your tone that you discovered my plans.<br><br>Do you have an issue with it, {HeroName}? You would have the highest honor, becoming one with me, with <i>Rularuu</i>, the most powerful being in the world.<br><br>Would you rather be part of the others, who would be slaves to our whims?"
// Page InformationPage1 SayOutLoudText :
"P3075346101" "Do you have an issue with my plan? You would have the highest honor, becoming one with me, with Rularuu the most powerful being in the world. Would you rather be part of the others, who would be slaves to our whims?"
// Answer Text :
"P2368740594" "I would rather have my freedom, Wade."
// Answer Text :
"P2264268155" "This was supposed to just be about taking down the Phalanx, Wade!"
// Answer Text :
"P61341905" "Still, it wouldn't be MY plan or MY goal Wade. It would be yours."
// Page Freedom Text :
"P3343554862" "Your <i>freedom</i>? {HeroName}, if you're not with me when I ascend, then you will have no freedom. Don't you understand?<br><br>No one in this world is truly free. There are always forces that can bend you, turn you to their will. Even Statesman here is not free.<br><br>I, {HeroName}, as a regular person, was never free. At any moment, some maniac with super powers could kill me. Can you imagine that?<br><br>After all the knowledge I obtained, all the experiences I had, some random punk with super strength could just flick his wrist and <i>kill</i> me!<br><br>But once I release Rularuu, once I <i>merge</i>, I will be <i>free</i>. No one will have the power to turn me to their will."
// Page Freedom SayOutLoudText :
"P4006084730" "Your freedom<? {HeroName}, if you're not with me when I ascend, then you will have no freedom. Don't you understand?"
// Answer Text :
"P3098278578" "Then that means I would still be beneath -you-, Wade."
// Page BeneathYou Text :
"P3232451083" "I suppose it does, but you would be above all the others of the world, {HeroName}!<br><br>I can already tell that this is not to your liking, is it? It's really too bad. You and I worked magnificently together. <br><br>I'll have to bring our work together to an end. You must realize, {HeroName}, that I have no choice but to eliminate you from the equation. I've come too far now to have someone like you stop me!"
// Page BeneathYou SayOutLoudText :
"P40324902" "I'll have to bring our work together to an end. You must realize, {HeroName}, that I have no choice but to eliminate you from the equation. I've come too far now to have someone like you stop me!"
// Answer Text :
"P2540143329" "Just try it, Wade!"
// Page TakingDownPhalanx Text :
"P2705910681" "The Phalanx were a means to an end, {HeroName}! That's what all people are, don't you see? Every person you meet, that you talk to, are a means to a greater goal that you have.<br><br>The death of Statesman wasn't the goal, it was a means to get us a point in time where I would have the power to become Rularuu!<br><br>And now, that goal is almost met. There is only one last person left in the equation, and that is Sister Psyche."
// Page TakingDownPhalanx SayOutLoudText :
"P410897597" "The Phalanx were a means to an end, {HeroName}! That's what all people are, don't you see? Every person you meet, that you talk to, are a means to a greater goal that you have."
// Answer Text :
"P3267323211" "You've gone too far, Wade. I can't let you go any further."
// Page GoFurther Text :
"P2062099102" "Your goals never matched mine, {HeroName}, I should have realized that from the start. But you can't stop what I've set in motion.<br><br>There are pieces and cogs which have already put into action events that will lead to one inevitable conclusion. And now, <i>you</i> seek to stop <i>me</i>, the man who has the power of Statesman?<br><br>Don't you see? You can't stop me now, {HeroName}. This is your last chance to change your mind. You can join me and become part of Rularuu when the world changes, or fall here, a mere blip on the radar of history."
// Page GoFurther SayOutLoudText :
"P1470287179" "Don't you see? You can't stop me now, {HeroName}. This is your last chance to change your mind. You can join me and become part of Rularuu when the world changes, or fall here, a mere blip on the radar of history."
// Answer Text :
"P3484435961" "I'll take option three, putting you down once and for all!"
// Page RunningtheShow Text :
"P1760309966" "Is it a matter of pride, {HeroName}? That I did what you could not? Many are going to be thinking that, of course. Yet, you have the distinct advantage of seeing exactly what <i>I</i> did.<br><br>Tell me, {HeroName}, do you intend to stop me now? Create a master plan to outwit my own so that you come out on top, that <i>you</i> emerge the bigger power in all of this?"
// Page RunningtheShow SayOutLoudText :
"P2839691993" "Is it a matter of pride, {HeroName}? That I did what you could not? Many are going to be thinking that, of course."
// Answer Text :
"P156914231" "That's one option, Wade. You could also stand down, make this easier."
// Page StandDown Text :
"P1412818755" "I've come too far to 'stand down'. Do you understand how many years of my life I've poured into this? The sacrifices I've made, both to my mind and my very soul itself?!<br><br>There is no turning back for me, {HeroName}. It is either this or nothing. I am the unstoppable force that will destroy anything that gets in the way of my lifelong goal. Do you intend to be the supposed immovable object to get in my way?<br><br>I should warn you, that you are <i>not</i> my equal. The only person who could be considered that is Lord Recluse, and even then, <i>that</i> is highly suspect."
// Page StandDown SayOutLoudText :
"P3524086833" "I've come too far to 'stand down'. Do you understand how many years of my life I've poured into this? The sacrifices I've made, both to my mind and my very soul itself?!"
// Answer Text :
"P3366610061" "We'll see about that, Wade!"
// Page Combat Text :
"P1425639219" "<color orange>Darrin Wade attacks you!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2425396993" "(Fight!)"

